  "slug": "quantum-topic-350f",
  "summary": "Six November 2026 preprints advance controlled, benchmarked approaches to open-system and many-body quantum dynamics beyond standard approximations.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the development of tractable, validated formalisms for quantum dynamics in regimes where standard approximations fail. Two papers address open-system descriptions: a nonsecular quantum master equation obeying TR-KMS detailed balance with a time-uniform O(λ²) error bound, and a transfer tensor generalization to time-inhomogeneous driven systems via block-TTI sub-stroboscopic sampling. Thermofield dynamics with ML-MCTDH and Bogoliubov transforms targets anharmonic (Morse) baths. A matrix-rational framework treats disorder-averaged spin density-matrix dynamics with generic spin-momentum couplings. The remaining two address many-body dynamics: generalized Bloch oscillations of a doublon defect in a 1D antiferromagnetic t-Jz chain, and adaptive ghost Gutzwiller dynamics matching DMFT references for Hubbard quenches over longer times. Common to most is explicit benchmarking against numerical or exact references.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
